# C3: the std submodules mlmf-conformance may name. DELIBERATELY EMPTY.
#
# The C3 purity gate scans `src/` only, and this crate's `src/lib.rs` is
# documentation with no code in it -- every line of this crate that does
# anything lives in `tests/`, which the gate does not scan. So there is
# nothing here to permit, and an entry added "just in case" would be a
# permission nobody re-examines.
#
# The file exists rather than being absent because `purity.rs::allowed_std`
# panics when a gated member does not declare a list. That is deliberate on
# its part: an absent file and an empty file would otherwise be
# indistinguishable, and the absent one would look like a crate nobody had
# considered.
